# Backend Folder Structure

Keep API code in this layout. Do not dump logic into `server.js` or invent parallel roots.

```
eezycycle-backend/
├── server.js                 # listen only — wire app, port
├── app.js                    # express app, middleware, mount routes
├── package.json
├── .env.example
├── config/                   # env, db, cors — no business logic
├── routes/                   # route tables only (thin)
├── controllers/              # req/res → call services
├── services/                 # business logic
├── repositories/             # MySQL queries / data access
├── middleware/               # auth, validate, error handler
├── utils/                    # shared helpers (error, logger, …)
├── validators/               # request schemas
├── sql/
│   ├── schema/               # CREATE TABLE scripts
│   ├── migrations/           # ordered ALTER scripts
│   └── seeds/                # optional seed data
└── tests/
```

## Placement rules

| Need | Put it in |
|------|-----------|
| New HTTP path | `routes/` + `controllers/` |
| Business rule / cycle math | `services/` |
| SQL / queries | `repositories/` + `sql/` |
| Shared helper used 2+ times | `utils/` |
| Express middleware | `middleware/` |
| Env / pool / constants | `config/` |

## Naming

- Files: `snake_case.js` (`cycle_service.js`, `error.js`)
- Classes/exports: `PascalCase` for types (`AppError`), `camelCase` for functions
- SQL: `001_create_users.sql`, `002_add_devices.sql` (ordered prefixes)

## Anti-patterns

- Fat `server.js` with routes + SQL + business logic
- Controllers talking to MySQL directly (skip `repositories/`)
- Duplicating `config` or env reads across files
- One-off `helpers/` / `lib/` / `common/` folders beside `utils/`
